diff --git a/debian/patches/0098-allow-vaapi-import-of-alpha-10-bit-rgb-drm-formats.patch b/debian/patches/0098-allow-vaapi-import-of-alpha-10-bit-rgb-drm-formats.patch
new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/debian/patches/0098-allow-vaapi-import-of-alpha-10-bit-rgb-drm-formats.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,59 @@
+Allow VAAPI to import the ALPHA spellings of the 10-bit RGB DRM formats.
+
+Vulkan exports a single-plane 10-bit RGB image as DRM_FORMAT_ARGB2101010 or
+DRM_FORMAT_ABGR2101010, never the X variants: hwcontext_vulkan.c's
+vkfmt_to_drmfmt() returns the first match in vulkan_drm_format_map, and that
+table lists the alpha spellings first --
+
+    { DRM_FORMAT_ARGB2101010, VK_FORMAT_A2B10G10R10_UNORM_PACK32 },
+    { DRM_FORMAT_ABGR2101010, VK_FORMAT_A2R10G10B10_UNORM_PACK32 },
+    { DRM_FORMAT_XRGB2101010, VK_FORMAT_A2B10G10R10_UNORM_PACK32 },
+    { DRM_FORMAT_XBGR2101010, VK_FORMAT_A2R10G10B10_UNORM_PACK32 },
+
+-- while vaapi_drm_format_map carries only the X spellings, patch 0038 having
+added X2B10G10R10 alongside upstream's X2R10G10B10. So mapping a Vulkan
+x2rgb10/x2bgr10 frame to VAAPI fails:
+
+    [AVHWFramesContext] DRM format not supported by VAAPI.
+    [Parsed_hwmap] Failed to map frame: -22.
+
+X and A differ only in whether the top two bits are meaningful; the memory
+layout is identical, and the driver accepts the surface either way -- verified
+on Mesa 26.0.4 / RX 9070 XT (gfx1201) before writing this:
+
+    -vf format=x2rgb10,hwupload,scale_vaapi=format=p010    rc=0
+
+Each alpha fourcc is mapped to the X fourcc of the SAME channel order, matching
+the pairing 0038 already established.
+
+Why it matters: it is the last thing between a VAAPI -> Vulkan -> VAAPI
+tonemapping chain and 10-bit output at full speed. On that hardware a MULTIPLANE
+Vulkan target (nv12, p010) costs ~2x -- measured 9.98 s against 19.46 s at equal
+bit depth, and the penalty follows the multiplane frame rather than the filter
+writing it -- so the fast chain must keep the Vulkan side single-plane. Today
+that forces 8-bit bgra and lets VAAPI's VPP widen to p010, which delivers the
+speed but only 8-bit precision. A single-plane 10-bit RGB target would keep both,
+and this is what blocks it.
+
+NOT addressed here: VA also advertises the alpha surface fourccs themselves
+(A2R10G10B10 / A2B10G10R10 show as "unknown" in vaapi_format_map). Naming them
+would need an alpha 10-bit RGB AVPixelFormat, which ffmpeg does not have, and
+nothing needs it -- the X mappings carry the same bytes.
+
+Index: FFmpeg/libavutil/hwcontext_vaapi.c
+===================================================================
+--- FFmpeg.orig/libavutil/hwcontext_vaapi.c
++++ FFmpeg/libavutil/hwcontext_vaapi.c
+@@ -1078,6 +1078,12 @@ static const struct {
+ #if defined(VA_FOURCC_X2B10G10R10) && defined(DRM_FORMAT_XBGR2101010)
+     DRM_MAP(X2B10G10R10, 1, DRM_FORMAT_XBGR2101010),
+ #endif
++#if defined(VA_FOURCC_X2R10G10B10) && defined(DRM_FORMAT_ARGB2101010)
++    DRM_MAP(X2R10G10B10, 1, DRM_FORMAT_ARGB2101010),
++#endif
++#if defined(VA_FOURCC_X2B10G10R10) && defined(DRM_FORMAT_ABGR2101010)
++    DRM_MAP(X2B10G10R10, 1, DRM_FORMAT_ABGR2101010),
++#endif
+ };
+ #undef DRM_MAP
+ 
